cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these certificates or the results of this paper, please cite it."
title: "The Koras-Russell cylinder as an affine modification of A^4: a commuting square through a motivic 4-sphere and a one-point Borel-Moore defect"
abstract: >-
  A global dissection of the Dubouloz-Moser-Jauslin-Poloni locally nilpotent
  derivation on the Koras-Russell cylinder, presenting the cylinder as a
  canonical affine modification of A^4 with a centre that cannot be rectified
  to a smooth one; a commuting square whose two intermediate models are the
  singular X_1 x A^1 and the smooth Y_1 = Q_{(3,1),z^2-1/4} of
  Asok-Dubouloz-Ostvaer; a four-corner motivic ledger in which the smooth
  route creates and then removes an L^2 packet; and, at integral Borel-Moore
  level, the identification of the generator of H^BM_4(Y_1;Z) with the
  fundamental class of either component of the doubled fibre, together with
  the explicit cycle that the modification destroys. Nothing is claimed about
  whether X x A^1 is isomorphic to A^4. All computational claims are
  machine-certified and reproducible from this repository.
